<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lê Thánh Tông</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1442–1497</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Le Thanh Tong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lê Thánh Tông was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s Later Lê dynasty from 1460 to 1497, its most celebrated ruler. He built a Confucian bureaucratic state with regular civil service examinations and reorganised provincial government. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-code">Hồng Đức code</a> was notable for protecting women's property rights. In 1471 he captured Vijaya, the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a>, and annexed much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cham">Cham</a> heartland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/le-thanh-tong.jpg" alt="Lê Thánh Tông" width="320" height="483" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ngoisao.vn · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L%C3%AA_Th%C3%A1nh_T%C3%B4ng.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
